      "mother": {
        "preparation": {
          "model_calls": 1,
          "phase": "preparation",
          "plan": {
            "A": "Optimize the exact dense DP in src/solution.cpp: use one contiguous in-place row, replace % MOD with conditional subtraction, and eliminate row copying. Research compact blocked-cell storage versus sorted per-row obstacle intervals so free runs avoid per-cell obstacle checks. Preserve initialization, duplicate obstacles, blocked endpoints, and n=1. Benchmark changes independently; this is the low-overhead baseline tree.",
            "B": "Research sparse-obstacle combinatorial DP: sort and deduplicate blocked coordinates, precompute factorials and inverse factorials through 2n-2, and subtract paths whose first blocked cell is each predecessor obstacle. Compute the destination similarly, modulo 1000000007, using safe 64-bit products. Complexity O(n+m^2) is attractive only for sufficiently sparse inputs; retain an exact dense fallback and determine crossover from measurements, not test identities.",
            "C": "Research exact parallel dense DP on four ARM64 cores using row-wise segmented modular prefix sums: each blocked cell resets the prefix, and the incoming left boundary propagates only until the first block in a chunk. Compare chunk summaries plus carry correction against a serial optimized kernel; avoid races and excessive per-row synchronization. Also investigate tiled wavefront scheduling if row barriers dominate. Keep parallelism only where measured worthwhile.",
            "G": "Integrate only validated programs from A/B/C. Compare standalone winners before combining; sparse dispatch and parallel thresholds must depend on legitimate dimensions, obstacle counts, and measured costs, never test identities. Retain the best serial fallback, deduplicate obstacles for sparse counting, and check n=1, empty obstacle sets, duplicate cells, blocked endpoints, and disconnected grids. Measure complete integrated execution repeatedly under the unchanged harness; integration gains are not assumed additive. Do not change compiler, tests, oracle, budgets, target, or permissions.",
            "analysis": "The supplied source targets Problem D, not the other three problems. It performs O(n^2) work, stores an n-by-n bit grid, copies each DP row, and computes a remainder per cell. Two reduced residues sum below signed 32-bit overflow, permitting conditional subtraction. The only measurement is a correct four-case baseline averaging 0.078851 seconds; there is no evidence about case dimensions or bottleneck distribution. Prioritize low-overhead serial improvements, investigate sparse combinatorial counting separately, and treat four-core parallelization as an experimentally justified alternative rather than an automatic gain. All approaches must preserve exact modular results for every valid input."
          },
